 ## Transport bar (`UMediaBoxTransportBar`, abstract `UUserWidget`)
 - Optional `BindWidgetOptional` parts: PlayPauseButton, StopButton, ScrubBar (Slider; pauses while dragged, plays on after), TimeText ("0:05 / 0:12", or elapsed only), VolumeSlider, MuteButton, SubtitlesButton (toggles the global switch), SubtitleText. Drives the box named Media Box around it (`MediaBoxFind::Find`), or Set Media Box. On Playing Changed / On Muted Changed for icons. The parts come from the user's own Widget Blueprint (GUID rule: nothing made in `OnCreationFromPalette`).
 
+## Media Box With Controls (`UMediaBoxWithControls`, `MediaBoxWithControls.h`)
+- **What:** a `UMediaBox` subclass with a controls bar over the video - a video player. Defaults: Visible (takes the pointer), Letterbox Color black, Desired Size 640 x 360.
+- **Bar:** `ControlsClass` (`TSubclassOf<UMediaBoxTransportBar>`), else Project Settings > Media Box > **Default Controls Class** (`TSoftClassPtr`), else none. Made in `RebuildWidget` with `CreateWidget(this, ...)` (designer flags copied in the designer), never added to the Widget Blueprint's tree (GUID rule); `SetMediaBox(this)`. Laid over the video in `SMediaBoxControlsHost` (private, in the .cpp): an `SOverlay` of the `SMediaBox` and the bar, `ControlsAlignment` (Bottom / Top...) stretched across, `ControlsPadding`. A new Controls Class takes effect when the widget is next built.
+- **Behaviour:** `bOverrideControlsBehavior` (inline toggle) + `ControlsBehavior`, else **Default Controls Behavior** in the settings. `FMediaBoxControlsBehavior` (`MediaBoxTypes.h`): `Preset` (`EMediaBoxControlsPreset`: YouTube / Custom; YouTube uses `YouTube()` whatever the fields hold, the fields greyed), Auto Hide, Hide After Idle (3 s), Hide After Unhovered (0.1 s), Show While Paused, Show While Stopped (also loading / ended), Show While Over Controls, Show While Focused, Show On Play / Pause, Fade In (0.1 s), Fade Out (0.25 s), Hide Pointer With Controls, Click To Play / Pause, Lift Subtitles. The defaults are the YouTube values.
+- **Tick** (`TickMediaBox` override, after the box's): hover from the host's `IsHovered`; activity = the pointer moving over it, entering it, a click, `ShowControls`, and (Show On Play / Pause) a status change. Playing: shown while over the controls / focused in them, else while hovered and active within Hide After Idle, else for Hide After Unhovered after leaving (and never past idle). Not playing: Show While Paused / Show While Stopped. Never hidden in the designer. The alpha fades by Fade In / Fade Out, goes to the bar's Render Opacity; at 0 the bar is Hidden (its own visibility back when shown). The pointer is `EMouseCursor::None` over the video while the bar is hidden. Lift Subtitles sets the box's `SubtitleBottomInset` (protected, new; 0 for a plain Media Box) to the bar's height x alpha when the bar is at the bottom.
+- **Click:** the host's `OnMouseButtonDown` (left, not over the bar) calls `TogglePlayPause` when Click To Play / Pause.
+- **Blueprint:** Get Controls, Show Controls, Are Controls Shown, Get Resolved Controls Behavior. Compiler note when there is no bar class at all.
